{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal","id":258,"title":"Scion: Origin - Whats the deal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-01T10:23:01-07:00","id":258,"title":"Scion: Origin - Whats the deal?","content":"Okay, so at Gencon, the rumors hold that Scion: Origin was discusses, and that the book covers a Scion's powers before their visitation. Pre-Hero stuff. I gotta ask, is this true? Because the entire appeal of Scion is the mythological stuff that takes over after the visitation. Anything set before that is going to be a pass for me, I'm in this for my mythic superhero pulp adventure that Scion 1.0 set up so readily. So, um. Some reassurance that we're getting a rad new edition of Scion and not Scion: Slightly Better Than A Mortal But You Ain't All That Yet edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/45-rainfall","name":"Rainfall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar45_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T10:27:18-07:00","id":264,"title":"","content":"<i>Scion: Origin</i> does indeed cover a Scion's life before Hero-hood. It will serve as the foundation book for the line, and be released at the same time as <i>Scion: Hero</i>. For any more details, we'll have to wait for a <i>Scion</i> writer or developer to pop in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T13:14:09-07:00","id":410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=264#post264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Scion: Origin</i> does indeed cover a Scion's life before Hero-hood. It will serve as the foundation book for the line, and be released at the same time as <i>Scion: Hero</i>. For any more details, we'll have to wait for a <i>Scion</i> writer or developer to pop in.</div> </div> </div> </div>So does this mean we need to get Scion: Origin as well as Scion: Hero to play the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is a signature &lt;-----------","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/118-shining-dragon","name":"Shining Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T14:21:22-07:00","id":481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shining Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=410#post410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So does this mean we need to get Scion: Origin as well as Scion: Hero to play the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but they'll be complete <i>settings</i> in their own right, even if they're not complete rulesets. <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ideally, Hero will be both a full mode of play and the first third of a heroic cycle, and a discussion on how your life changes when your blood turns to ichor. Demigod will build on that foundation, but will also be a full game in its own right. Our goal is to clean, build and expand upon the experience of the first edition of Scion, with Origin underlying the entirety of the line and providing a setting and mechanical backbone so we don't have to explain it all in Hero.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Origin</b><br /> <br /> We're still largely deciding what goes into Origin and what goes into Hero, but the idea is that the bare bones of the mechanical system will be laid out in Origin. <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The book can be used to create and play urban fantasy stories, and will include the setting(s) for doing just that. If creatures are handled in the book, they'll be beings of myth but low Legend - dryads, satyrs, and the like. And, yes, pre-Visitation Scions, but also holy men and women of the pantheons, sorcerers who seek to steal the power of the gods, and those bound by Fate (your Oedipuses, your Cassandras, your Arjunas). Some of its mechanics will include not just the baseline rules, but also rules for things that cross over and access all three tiers of play - magic and Fate among them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Hero</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hero will include rules on taking characters from the SCR and giving them their first dot of Legend, with all the powers and Purviews that come with that. Not having to cram a full rule-set into this book means that we've got more space in which to play with things, including a nice, fat variety of powers, and other elements that are Hero-specific. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is also where you'll see the full mechanical concept of our scaling system, which affects all four books. Moo hoo hah hah!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It also means that we've got space for a big catalog of pantheons, since the basics have been covered in Origin. The original six are returning (though we're talking about heavily changing the Loa), </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">going into more depth than Hero 1e did.</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> I'll ask him if we can spoil the rest (since we're talking about more). Ideally, Joe would like to touch on multiple other pantheons per book.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Demigod</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Demigod will include rules for bringing our heroes into the Divine tier, including the ability to Invoke their...well, that'd be spoiling too much. Suffice it to say what we're talking about includes stuff on how pantheons are formed, <i>what </i>pantheons actually are, and an exegesis of stuff like <i>interpretatio romana</i>. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It's definitely going to contain rules for play in mid-to-high Myth locales, such as Touchstones, Terra Incognita and the like, as well as Underworlds; and, of course, demigod powers. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b>God</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rules for bringing our heroes into the Empyrean tier, with all the power and responsibilities that assumes. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">More material for play in high-Myth locales, particularly Titan-Realms and Firmaments. And, yes, rules to shake the cosmos and the foundations of Fate.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T16:24:08-07:00","id":654,"title":"","content":"Okay that sounds perfect. My fears are neatly allayed and I will commence being absurdly excited once again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/45-rainfall","name":"Rainfall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar45_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T16:51:23-07:00","id":694,"title":"","content":"So they're completely rebooting the Game &amp; System? Also will we be able to use stuff from the Scion Companion of the prior edition ( well the basic fluff info) in some of the Sidebars ect as well as the gods--- to audgment this new edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":205,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/205-songtress","user":"Songtress","date":". 11-01-2013, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/205-songtress","name":"Songtress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar205_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T17:20:31-07:00","id":713,"title":"","content":"That sounds very promising! About this scaling system: will it affect the likes of dryads and satyrs and such? Could you play such a creature in a game that advances into Hero and beyond?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T18:05:48-07:00","id":740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Songtress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=694#post694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they're completely rebooting the Game &amp; System? Also will we be able to use stuff from the Scion Companion of the prior edition ( well the basic fluff info) in some of the Sidebars ect as well as the gods--- to augment this new edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no, respectively. Game and system are being completely rewritten. One of our goals (bolded up in top of our design docs, repeated at every design meeting) is to ensure the good experiences people loved in Scion 1.0 still have a major place in 2.0. You won't be able to use artifacts or gods-as-written, though you could absolutely convert things over, and some of the design decisions that the previous authors made will be carried forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T19:30:01-07:00","id":801,"title":"","content":"I am super-excited. I always though it was really lame that witches, sorcerers and other non-Legendary beings didnt exist AT ALL in Scion. Origin might offer an alternative to things like Adventure! and allow for more pulpy, Jonny-Quest style games.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: I will say that I hope satyrs, drayds, elves and dwarves <b>aren't</b> playable &quot;races&quot;. Scion should be about Scions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","user":"Telgar","date":".  addin stuff 11-01-2013, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T19:49:02-07:00","id":814,"title":"","content":"What are the odds of an Abrahamic Pantheon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T20:17:52-07:00","id":839,"title":"","content":"Man... zero, I hope. Abrahamic religions don't have a Pantheon, they're monotheists. Pantheon means multiple Gods and that's the opposite of monotheism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T20:31:02-07:00","id":862,"title":"","content":"There are valid reasons to believe there were at one point polytheistic Abrahamic faiths* with a polytheistic approach, though none currently exist that I'm aware of. It is also unclear how different those would have been from other polytheistic Semitic faiths, which I would love to see some attention but are probably better served from the perspective of Babylonia, whose polytheistic pantheons are better documented.<br /> <br /> (* the old testament is unclear on the matter of multiple gods and there are valid interpretations of multiple segments to be implying the existence of multiple gods. Likewise, the biblical tendency of the Israelian people to turn to polytheism shows that to the Israelian people of those times, it certainly wasn't that strange a leap to their mindset.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />All who wish to exist must first accept the existence of things beyond themselves and their current awareness, only then can existence return the favour.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://webchat.sorcery.net/?channels=theonyxpath\" target=\"_blank\">irc.sorcery.net #theonyxpath</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/236-ina","name":"Ina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar236_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T20:33:05-07:00","id":863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=839#post839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man... zero, I hope. Abrahamic religions don't have a Pantheon, they're monotheists. Pantheon means multiple Gods and that's the opposite of monotheism.</div> </div> </div> </div>There could easily be a quasi-Pantheon of Archangels or other important figures in the religion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T20:35:35-07:00","id":866,"title":"","content":"Let's not get into that argument on these nice clean new forums, okay? Or at the very least, start a new thread rather than derail this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T20:40:07-07:00","id":870,"title":"","content":"A &quot;pantheon&quot; of angels presents a problem: it presumes the existence of God. A God who really, truly, totally, is MORE Godly than the other Gods. Who is head and shoulders above everyone else in the setting. That's goes against everything else in the setting. <br /> <br /> Now a Caananite Pantheon, that has Baal, Dagon, Moloch, Astarte, etc, that could be really cool. But a Pantheon of Lucifer, Jesus, Mary, Gabriel, etc? No, no thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T20:44:06-07:00","id":872,"title":"","content":"Who's to say God is more Godly than the other Gods in the setting of Scion? He'd be just as Godly as Izanagi or Baron Samedi<br /> <br /> But I'm really vibing on your Caananite Pantheon idea, man. I didn't even think about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T20:59:08-07:00","id":881,"title":"","content":"*takes out a stopwatch* That didn't take long at all.<br /> <br /> Back to the topic at hand, I am SUPER EXCITED about the coordination present here. I loved Scion, but it was kind of a hot mess, and I'd like to not have to cobble together mechanics with shoelaces and dreams. Also digging the idea that Origin can provide a Legendless version of Scion for those who prefer lower-powered games.<br /> <br /> I'm happy the core six are returning (particularly the Aztecs, and especially that the Loa are being overhauled). Any ballpark estimates to the number of pantheons we might get? I really want me some Inca","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T21:01:44-07:00","id":883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=872#post872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's to say God is more Godly than the other Gods in the setting of Scion? He'd be just as Godly as Izanagi or Baron Samedi<br /> <br /> But I'm really vibing on your Caananite Pantheon idea, man. I didn't even think about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically I named that first (the Babylonian Pantheon was essentially identical to the Canaanite one, the differences we're aware of smaller than the difference between the Roman and Greek pantheons.)<br /> <br /> Polytheistic Semitic faiths are interesting, such a shame they died when Zoroastrianism, Christianity and Islam started to popularise monotheism in a form that wasn't bound tightly to a single ethnicity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />All who wish to exist must first accept the existence of things beyond themselves and their current awareness, only then can existence return the favour.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://webchat.sorcery.net/?channels=theonyxpath\" target=\"_blank\">irc.sorcery.net #theonyxpath</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/236-ina","name":"Ina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar236_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T21:04:22-07:00","id":884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=883#post883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically I named that first (the Babylonian Pantheon was essentially identical to the Canaanite one, the differences we're aware of smaller than the difference between the Roman and Greek pantheons.)<br /> <br /> Polytheistic Semitic faiths are interesting, such a shame they died when Zoroastrianism, Christianity and Islam started to popularise monotheism in a form that wasn't bound tightly to a single ethnicity.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, must have missed your post, probably glossed over it cause no profile picture. But you did definitely mention it first. Kudos to you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T21:06:06-07:00","id":887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the odds of an Abrahamic Pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hotly debated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=801#post801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I will say that I hope satyrs, drayds, elves and dwarves <b>aren't</b> playable &quot;races&quot;. Scion should be about Scions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, the focus is on replicating the experience - but then, things are still in flux at this stage, and it's never wise to close a door too firmly when you might need to walk through it later. <b>Exalted</b> was about the Exalted, but God-Blooded, Heroic Ghosts, Dragon-Kings - they're fan favorites, and they even made an appearance in the 2e corebook. Dryads and nymphs and elementals and kami were the children of the gods, too. Aren't they scions by another name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":".  Sneaky sneaky 11-02-2013, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T21:30:30-07:00","id":898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=881#post881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to not have to cobble together mechanics with shoelaces and dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, aren't they all?<br /> <br /> You won't, though. A tight system is a big focus point for us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm happy the core six are returning (particularly the Aztecs, and especially that the Loa are being overhauled). Any ballpark estimates to the number of pantheons we might get? I really want me some Inca </div> </div> </div>I <i>could</i> give you a ballpark estimate, but I'm not going to, lest Joe maul me. I will say that the additional (new, rather than Companion) pantheons we're batting around for inclusion are all over the globe in terms of locations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 11-02-2013, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T21:52:49-07:00","id":905,"title":"","content":"Caananite and Babylonian have distinct mythologies, though there are some similarities between them as there are with the Norse and the Greeks. Babylonian and Assyrian and Akkadian and Sumerian are all much closer together, but the Canaanite/Phoenician group is fairly distinct from them. <br /> <br /> As for polytheisitic Semitic faiths, there also the pre-Islamic Arabian Gods. The folks at GBN have fan-published Pantheons for the Elohim (Canaanite), the Anunna (Babylonian) and the Alihah (Arabian). They're pretty good. <br /> <br /> I just can't get behind the idea of playing a Son of Jesus or a Daughter of Satan in Scion. It's got such a different feel. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T22:50:45-07:00","id":917,"title":"","content":"I am hoping for more Pantheons. in other books, perhaps the 'The Great Book of Pantheons!&quot; series ( so they could do a lot of pantheons that could give a lot of flavor and life to other pantheons that are outside the 'main pantheons' . I loved the Companion pantheons it was a good start. Plenty of goood side information in those. Though I do wonder if the Deities of Scion 2.0 willl be able to leave a little bit of divine in their mortal-avatar(?) and raise the child. <br /> <br /> I always felt strange saying that this kid got adopted or sometihng ( admited one of my Scions was the child of two 'scions' her self ( one her parents slept with the approprietely gendered deitey) but the two scions were married couple and raised the girl as their daughter...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/205-songtress","name":"Songtress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar205_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T23:19:30-07:00","id":940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=887#post887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, the focus is on replicating the experience - but then, things are still in flux at this stage, and it's never wise to close a door too firmly when you might need to walk through it later. <b>Exalted</b> was about the Exalted, but God-Blooded, Heroic Ghosts, Dragon-Kings - they're fan favorites, and they even made an appearance in the 2e corebook. Dryads and nymphs and elementals and kami were the children of the gods, too. Aren't they scions by another name?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pickin' up what you're layin' down, man. Groovy.<br /> <br /> ... I'd like to see some of these creatures be playable in such a game. More mythology is always a good thing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T00:02:21-07:00","id":964,"title":"","content":"I am reposting this again in bold and redtext because apparently some people didn't see it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=866#post866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Let's not get into that argument [viability of Abrahamic Pantheon] on these nice clean new forums, okay? Or at the very least, start a new thread rather than derail this one</span>.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T00:45:53-07:00","id":978,"title":"","content":"Are there any plans for books beyond the core four, or is that still in flux?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T01:22:05-07:00","id":989,"title":"","content":"Not yet, but the opposite isn't true either. Scion 1E was designed as a limited run. Scion 2E isn't, it's just that we're still writing the first book, let alone thinking about what happens after the fourth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T07:47:00-07:00","id":1090,"title":"","content":"...how on Earth did Ina comment just on Dave's post? What's going on?! This forum is a strange and alien vista to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T10:05:16-07:00","id":1140,"title":"","content":"I for one am looking forward to an updated Tuatha with a more balanced PSP. Neall, I too like the idea of being able to play the children of god+elf or god+nymph as it is solidly found in the myths to begin with and could add some interesting character options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">At the end of the day, what works in <b>YOUR</b> story with <b>YOUR</b> players is what matters most. Not what someone on some forum says.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/328-phoenixfire","name":"PhoenixFire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar328_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T10:42:01-07:00","id":1157,"title":"","content":"I could see human+nymph, like Achilles, but God+Elf would (should) be a Lesser Immortal, not a Scion. Scions need that spark of humanity to be super-special-awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T11:43:56-07:00","id":1188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=839#post839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man... zero, I hope. Abrahamic religions don't have a Pantheon, they're monotheists. Pantheon means multiple Gods and that's the opposite of monotheism.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if we follow that we cut out the Loa as well, since the only true god in Voodoo/Vodun is Bondye, with the Loa holding a position closer to the angels or saints in some forms of Christianity, and act on Bondye's behalf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T12:01:08-07:00","id":1194,"title":"","content":"Ahem. Abrahamic pantheon in another thread before Ian gets ticked off, please? This is a useful thread, and I'd hate to get it derailed because people keep missing Ian's warning.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Check that, I'll start it myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 11-02-2013, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T14:28:35-07:00","id":1303,"title":"","content":"I was about to be super-cynical about Origins, but now, i'm pretty damn pumped. I really like the idea of having a &quot;mechanics&quot; centric book in Origins so that the others can have more information and character options. I also tend to like going somewhat humanity-centric in my Scion gaming, so the idea of having Scion, the Urban Fantasy, as a low power level, sounds really attractive to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T19:07:06-08:00","id":2291,"title":"","content":"I am definitely excited about this....especially with the fact that Origin and Hero will be out at the same time. Neall, I know there's a chance you may not be able to say anything but with the possible redesign for the Loa, would that include elements of the Orishas or are you referring to something else entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/601-dioscuri","name":"Dioscuri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T21:26:53-08:00","id":2361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=866#post866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not get into that argument on these nice clean new forums, okay? Or at the very least, start a new thread rather than derail this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Superheroes? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T22:29:05-08:00","id":2399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=2361#post2361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Superheroes? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Superheroes explicitly go against the stated goals of the game in that they are MODERN myth and Scion is a game about bringing ancient myth forward into the modern world.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say that superheroes wouldn't fit into the world of Scion, but there's no way they'd blend in with the other published material, and licensing fees for Marvel/DC superheroes would be absolutely silly and doing a pantheon of off-brand superheroes would feel immensely cheap. You'll be a lot better off making a Fantheon of your own for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/45-rainfall","name":"Rainfall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar45_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T22:30:22-08:00","id":2400,"title":"","content":"I am hesitantly optimistic about Scion: Origins. In general I do not have much use for a legendless system, and prefer to head directly to Demigod as fast as reasonably possible. However, I have the sneaking suspicion that Scion: Origins and Scion: Hero will have strong parallels to World of Darkness Core and Vampire: the Masquerade in function.<br /> <br /> That is to say, it sounds like Scion: Origins will be a core mechanical book for mundane people adventuring in a mythical world. Then Scion: Hero will be a specific splat within the world of Scion: Origins.<br /> <br /> This leaves the door open to future publications involving other supernatural creatures that might also fit within the mythical world of Scion: Origins. These other splats might have parallels in function to Werewolf or Mage, and get their own 1 to 3 book runs if the Hero / Demigod / God books sell well enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T22:38:35-08:00","id":2403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rainfall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=2399#post2399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Superheroes explicitly go against the stated goals of the game in that they are MODERN myth and Scion is a game about bringing ancient myth forward into the modern world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. It's also the most reasonable and polite response I've gotten on that matter, especially in the old forum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which isn't to say that superheroes wouldn't fit into the world of Scion, but there's no way they'd blend in with the other published material, and licensing fees for Marvel/DC superheroes would be absolutely silly and doing a pantheon of off-brand superheroes would feel immensely cheap. </div> </div> </div>Look me in the eye and tell me you wouldn't want to play a game in which you face off with the deadly Scions of Brick-Bat.0<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You'll be a lot better off making a Fantheon of your own for them. </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Though I'm not really sure I could bring myself to do what it takes to build Kirby's Fourth World characters as Scion ones. Because that means making at least one of the Antagonists a Titan and if I do it the Terrorists will have won.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 12-23-2013, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T10:49:25-08:00","id":2768,"title":"","content":"Alright! Here's my debut post in the new forums!<br /> <br /> Anyways, I'm super-excited now about Scion: Origins. I had a few reservations, but our great devs pretty much just killed them all in this one thread.<br /> <br /> I'm very pleased to hear that Origin and Hero are coming out together. My biggest gripe was that I may have to wait several months before my friends and I can actually start playing as Scions. Excellent call to release them together, devs!<br /> <br /> Words cannot express how THRILLED I am to hear about sorcerers and witches who try to steal power from the gods. I DO believe that Scions shouldn't be too threatened by mortals, but I am a firm believer that not every threat a Scion faces should be creatures of Legend. I think this will add a new level of depth and complexity to a game line that sorely needs such things. Once again, I can't thank you guys enough for this one!<br /> <br /> And finally? I couldn't be happier to hear that Scion, this time, isn't being planned as a limited run. I firmly believe that Scion can, and should, be just as big as Exalted, and I'm thrilled to hear that this time it might actually get a legitimate shot at that. Obviously, sales figures will be the real deciding factor here, but I'm very happy to see that Onyx Path is willing to give Scion a real chance at becoming a big-time franchise.<br /> <br /> I seriously have no worries at all at this time. My only source of agitation comes exclusively from waiting for more information about this great game line. And, of course, the wait until I can get my hands on Origin and Hero is going to drive me nuts! But I strongly believe I'm going to find it to be well worth the wait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T11:37:10-08:00","id":2800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=1090#post1090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...how on Earth did Ina comment just on Dave's post? What's going on?! This forum is a strange and alien vista to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah how do you comment on posts?<br /> <br /> Anyway I'm really excited as Scion is what got me to reading WW stuff in the first place, I cant wait to see the new system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T19:40:52-08:00","id":3108,"title":"","content":"I'm a little leery on Origins as a stand alone game itself. The whole interest for me is the child of a god mythology behind the game. But, the notion that its baseline rules book leaving more room for setting materials and mythology in Hero, I can get behind that. I eagerly await to see what's coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T08:29:32-08:00","id":3516,"title":"","content":"I agree wholeheartedly. I got the sense that the other starter books were missing certain gods in the core pantheons that never showed up in other supplements (Khonsu, Hestia, etc).<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of fleshing out mortal servitors like sorcerers and such since those are a key point in any cthonic cult (just look at lovecraft fiction).<br /> <br /> Think they'll leave Raiden as a god and add his brother Fujin or make both of them Titan avatars since they're both actually big oni?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":765,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","user":"Darksol-aeternium","date":". 11-05-2013, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T06:24:34-08:00","id":4255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=740#post740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and no, respectively. Game and system are being completely rewritten. One of our goals (bolded up in top of our design docs, repeated at every design meeting) is to ensure the good experiences people loved in Scion 1.0 still have a major place in 2.0. You won't be able to use artifacts or gods-as-written, though you could absolutely convert things over, and some of the design decisions that the previous authors made will be carried forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly hope that the design decisions being carried forward don't include that &quot;Pan is now the devil&quot; crap from the first one. Don't get me wrong, it was a clever way to tie an ancient mythological figure in with one that is more frequently considered in the modern day, but the story of the flaying was the myth of Marsyas, not Pan. It left me with the impression that in the design process, somebody said, &quot;Hey, this myth would be great to build off of for a plot point involving an ancient figure embracing the mythology of Satan in order to empower themselves, but instead of going with Marsyas, why don't we call him Pan, because they're both depicted as satyrs, but Pan is a name that more people would recognize.&quot; I would love to see Pan treated as an actual God in the new Scion, with his own scions (maybe even ones among the satyrs themselves), and leave the myth of Marsyas to Marsyas (who could easily have been treated as a Demigod level scion of Pan in the first place). <br /> <br /> All that said, I am eagerly looking forward to the new Scion, because so far, I am loving everything I'm hearing about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T10:02:37-08:00","id":4436,"title":"","content":"What sorts of precautions are being taken to ensure that power level scales better than it did in 1e? I'm not saying that a hero should ever be able to defeat a demigod in the demigod's area of expertise, but a one or two legend difference also shouldn't be a nearly guaranteed loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T10:32:35-08:00","id":4455,"title":"","content":"I suspect questions like that are the purview of system details we don't yet have. What we do know is that a better scaling of power level is a deliberate design goal this time around specifically so that the kind of situation you're talking about doesn't come up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T13:59:22-08:00","id":4576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James McMurray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=4436#post4436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sorts of precautions are being taken to ensure that power level scales better than it did in 1e? I'm not saying that a hero should ever be able to defeat a demigod in the demigod's area of expertise, but a one or two legend difference also shouldn't be a nearly guaranteed loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it was hardly ever a guaranteed loss for reasons I have elaborated upon many times in the old forums. It would certainly help to better balance the various dice adders and how they play into defensive equations, of course.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T13:59:46-08:00","id":4577,"title":"","content":"Looking forward to seeing the new interpretation. Origins has me intrigued, Mortals happens to be my favorite line in nWoD. Some things I'd like to see are the inclusion of aspirations/conditions and experience like in GMC, a clearer Antagonist creation system as opposed to a set bestiary, Mythic Age setting at some point ala Dark Ages/Rome etc, have more than one boon at a given level in a purview and purchase them like WW gifts, in addition to expanding birthrights I'd to see merits or backgrounds added.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/783-xsv-violence","name":"Xsv-Violence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T11:07:04-08:00","id":8234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=887#post887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, the focus is on replicating the experience - but then, things are still in flux at this stage, and it's never wise to close a door too firmly when you might need to walk through it later. <b>Exalted</b> was about the Exalted, but God-Blooded, Heroic Ghosts, Dragon-Kings - they're fan favorites, and they even made an appearance in the 2e corebook. Dryads and nymphs and elementals and kami were the children of the gods, too. Aren't they scions by another name?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m glad to hear this. Personally, I\u2019ve always been a fan of scions getting center stage, but <i>not</i> being the <i>exclusive</i> protagonists of the game. To me, the main draw of <b>Scion</b> is the fidelity of its modeling of real-world mythologies, and the \u201cchildren of the gods\u201d thing is of secondary importance; and I don\u2019t want to be told that I\u2019m playing it wrong if I choose to center a chronicle around sorcerers, holy men, amazons, nymphs, kami, or other mythological beings. <br /> <br /> Besides, it\u2019s a lot easier for a Storyteller who wants to focus exclusively on scions to forbid non-scion protagonists that the game otherwise permits than it is for a Storyteller who wants to focus on other character types that the game relegates entirely to the role of supporting cast to do so: the latter has to hand-craft the rules needed to do so; the former need only ignore the rules he doesn\u2019t want to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T03:19:57-08:00","id":28609,"title":"","content":"So Scion 2E will follow the WW model where the first book was about the Mortals (aka what happened before the player got Embraced, Changed, Awakened, etc.) Will Scion 2E also have the same requisite of needing Origins as well as one of the other books to play or are they separate parts of the game like 1st Edition was?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T06:53:59-08:00","id":28691,"title":"","content":"Origins is like the new World of Darkness; you need Origins because it has the core rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T11:42:01-08:00","id":28843,"title":"","content":"Well, we don't know. It is possible that, like with Dark Ages Revised, the core rules get released later so that you don't have to have the full Origins book with you if you're focusing on the other tiers of play. You'd still need a separate book/document, but given that unlike the nWOD core book (which is very heavy on the rules and very light on anything else) Origin will be a bit more extensive of a game by itself, I can see it being viable for core rules of Scion 2e to be something that gets separated out it we voice enough interest in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T12:16:58-08:00","id":28872,"title":"","content":"Well, first of all i'd like to thank the developers who are taking their time to write information; Scion is one of my dearest rpgs, and all the information we are having access to is getting me fearful, because it sounds TOO GOOD to be true. Do you know one thing i'd like to see? Scions not made by pure f*ck action. I mean, what if somebody, one human, would have mastered such proficiency in some area that one god or goddess felt compelled to claim him/her as an offspring? I think that would be interesting. Shows the inherent potential in humans, after all. We're all the children of the Gods, at some point or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T13:35:16-08:00","id":28902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=28843#post28843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we don't know. It is possible that, like with Dark Ages Revised, the core rules get released later so that you don't have to have the full Origins book with you if you're focusing on the other tiers of play. You'd still need a separate book/document, but given that unlike the nWOD core book (which is very heavy on the rules and very light on anything else) Origin will be a bit more extensive of a game by itself, I can see it being viable for core rules of Scion 2e to be something that gets separated out it we voice enough interest in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see the need for that? I mean everyone was an ordinary mortal at some point in Scion, before Visitation. Origins is the logical point to put the core rules that form the foundation of the whole game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T14:34:33-08:00","id":28933,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying the Origins shouldn't contain the core rules. I'm saying that Onyx Path could release the rules by themselves as a separate PDF (again this is what happened with Dark Ages Revised, or could be compared to the free GMC rules update PDF) for people that want the rules without having everything else in Origins with them when they're playing Demigod level games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T19:04:25-08:00","id":29081,"title":"","content":"Unlike Dark Ages, where the rules were all in Vampire and you had to buy Vampire even if this had no relevance to your Dark Ages game, Origins is nowhere near that same level of potential irrelevance to a Demigod game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T21:41:07-08:00","id":29144,"title":"","content":"I'm still not getting your resistance to the concept. Neither of knows at this point how reasonable/feasible/important it could be. We don't know how much a Demigod level game is going to want to reference the non-core-rules sections of Origin.<br /> <br /> I could be wrong and it could be pointless. Or I could be right and it could be a valuable tool for people playing higher tier games. But it isn't like it would actually harm anything if the core-rules were distilled out. The only question is if it would be beneficial, which will have to wait for at least Demigod to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T23:44:24-08:00","id":29178,"title":"","content":"We won\u2019t know until <b>Scion: Origins</b> is published; but I suspect that, like the World of Darkness core rulebook, something like 90% to 99% of <b>Origins</b> will be relevant to Heroes, Demigods, and even Gods. Certainly, <b>Scion</b> has a precedent for this sort of thing: you can\u2019t really play a god without owning <b>Scion: Hero</b> and <b>Scion: Demigod</b> as well as <b>Scion: God</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T07:33:37-08:00","id":30414,"title":"","content":"10 Pantheons in one Book, wow thats nice ! So the 6 starter are included and the other 4? Are they the Companion ones and Yazata or do we get something different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T05:37:40-08:00","id":31603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeadGuy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=30414#post30414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10 Pantheons in one Book, wow thats nice ! So the 6 starter are included and the other 4? Are they the Companion ones and Yazata or do we get something different?</div> </div> </div> </div> The original six pantheons (altered a bit, though) plus four more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T07:04:17-08:00","id":31632,"title":"","content":"o...so coy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T10:59:46-08:00","id":32574,"title":"","content":"Well, I should hope the original 6 pantheons get a little revision. At the very least, some of the old Purview associations were, well, slipshod (a subject on which many of us can and have discoursed at tedious length). <br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T19:16:38-08:00","id":32912,"title":"","content":"revision, renaming, refocusing\u2026 I\u2019m optimistic, considering who is being consulted. (Renaming: Dodekatheon -&gt; Theoi; refocusing: Loa-&gt;Orisha.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T05:56:23-08:00","id":33101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=32912#post32912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">revision, renaming, refocusing\u2026 I\u2019m optimistic, considering who is being consulted. (Renaming: Dodekatheon -&gt; Theoi; refocusing: Loa-&gt;Orisha.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been very much on the fence about renaming the pantheons to those specific words. Especially because it can create confusion when the gods of any given region would refer to everyone by those names and not just their own region. While none of the options fit perfectly for me, I think 'naming' them by their region would be a lot easier to reference both OOC and IC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T22:37:06-08:00","id":33711,"title":"","content":"I mostly agree with you Iry. I think region names are probably &quot;best&quot; but again, confusing cause what do modern names of regions really mean? My preference is something like:<br /> <br /> Theoi<br /> The Gods of Greece<br /> <br /> As a heading for each pantheon. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1051-jsr","name":"JSR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T22:37:44-08:00","id":33712,"title":"","content":"Also this is john talking, anne is asleep and prefers the other way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1051-jsr","name":"JSR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T03:18:31-08:00","id":33772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JSR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=33711#post33711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly agree with you Iry. I think region names are probably &quot;best&quot; but again, confusing cause what do modern names of regions really mean? My preference is something like:<br /> <br /> Theoi<br /> The Gods of Greece<br /> <br /> As a heading for each pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I do not think there is any solution that does not break a few eggs. We could say 'Egyptian Gods' when referencing the ancient Egyptians, but the region is predominantly Muslim at the moment. Things get even more messy if we reference areas with several pantheons and heavy syncretization such as Castile or the Berbers.<br /> <br /> I could definitely get behind <u>&quot;Theoi, the Gods of Greece&quot;</u> as a pretty descriptive name that touches the most important points.. It might be too long for banners of course!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T05:31:56-08:00","id":33801,"title":"","content":"Considering the audience that is mostly western-centric, I think it'd be wise to keep what we already know. The very word &quot;Egypt&quot; likely conjures ancient imagery rather than what is currently prevalent. The same applies for other cultural geographical areas. I already just kind of...skip dodeka...whatever when ever I see the word, and replace it with the word &quot;Greek.&quot; To me, Greece is Zeus, Hera, Apollo, Herakles, Hermes, etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T09:39:22-08:00","id":33914,"title":"","content":"We never used that clumsy word &quot;Dodecatheon&quot; in any of my home games. We simply replaced it with the word &quot;Olympians&quot; whether or not it was accurate. I had a person who actually studied Ancient Greek as a language and he never complained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T09:42:31-08:00","id":33916,"title":"","content":"Olympians IS a bit more accurate, even if not completely. Theoi is best. I like keeping linguistically-appropriate names. It doesn't make anything less useful, it just adds some flavor to descriptions. There's &quot;Norse Gods&quot;, sure, but Aesir has some oomph to it. It's what an Aesir would call themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T10:33:13-08:00","id":33952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=33916#post33916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Olympians IS a bit more accurate, even if not completely. Theoi is best. I like keeping linguistically-appropriate names. It doesn't make anything less useful, it just adds some flavor to descriptions. There's &quot;Norse Gods&quot;, sure, but Aesir has some oomph to it. It's what an Aesir would call themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely think that is what the Aesir would call themselves, but certainly not what Njord, Nerthus, Freyr, Freya, Aegir, Ran, Hel, or the Norns would call themselves.<br /> <br /> I definitely think Theoi is what the Greeks would call themselves, but they would also use Theoi to describe the Norse, Celtic, Egyptian, Mexica, Chinese, Russian, Japanese, Australian, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T11:10:44-08:00","id":33970,"title":"","content":"Hel's an Aesir. The others are Vanir, but some (Freyr, Freya) are assimilated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T11:48:35-08:00","id":33991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=33970#post33970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hel's an Aesir. The others are Vanir, but some (Freyr, Freya) are assimilated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember them ever claiming she was an Aesir, just like they did not claim Fenrir or Jormungandr were Aesir. But maybe I overlooked something? Do you have a line from one of the Eddas?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T03:46:33-08:00","id":35493,"title":"","content":"I really hope the Devas are one of the core 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/480-blind-dragon","name":"Blind Dragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T15:48:33-08:00","id":35862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=1157#post1157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see human+nymph, like Achilles, but God+Elf would (should) be a Lesser Immortal, not a Scion. Scions need that spark of humanity to be super-special-awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sun Wukong says &quot;Na-a-aw&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless you really want to call the Great Sage Equaling Heaven a &quot;lesser&quot; anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T16:05:48-08:00","id":35874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=35862#post35862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sun Wukong says &quot;Na-a-aw&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless you really want to call the Great Sage Equaling Heaven a &quot;lesser&quot; anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shen: Okay! Lesser-than-humble! Beat that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T16:29:01-08:00","id":35901,"title":"","content":"Sun Wukong was never a Scion. He would never have been treated as one. He was a magical monkey that followed Taoist practices to achieve godly power. Taoist mythology is full of that, it's a core feature of the religion. Tao hard enough and become immortal. The Eight Immortals did it. The Monkey King did it. They're not Scions. They're Gods. What were they originally? Hard to say. But they weren't Scions, since they didn't have a Godly parent.<br /> <br /> No game system can represent every single religious story ever. I have never claimed that Scion can, or should. In fact, I claim the opposite. Scion has to be internally consistent, elegant and simple. It has to make choices and say &quot;X is X, Y is Y and that's that.&quot; Scions are part human, part god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T16:48:09-08:00","id":35914,"title":"","content":"In the context of Scion, I'd argue that Sun Wukong started out as a Titanspawn who converted either through Subhuti's teachings or upon reaching the Pure Land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T17:03:05-08:00","id":35924,"title":"","content":"Just to add a third voice of dissention, Sun Wukong is an example of a god that was never a Scion and never ought to have been. Shen in general tend to be something of &quot;The Other, exalted.&quot; More than most other pantheons likely to make it into Scion, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T17:12:57-08:00","id":35928,"title":"","content":"The further you get from Western Culture, the less myths fit into Scion's boxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T20:49:15-08:00","id":36066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=35901#post35901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion has to be internally consistent, elegant and simple. It has to make choices and say &quot;X is X, Y is Y and that's that.&quot; Scions are part human, part god.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because something is complicated, does not mean it cannot be elegant and exactingly consistent.<br /> <img src=\"https://encrypted-tbn2.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRZXr4GogZe5HN30e5bIuNBLFs4SpYigCu8hir5BElMFJl0tHjx\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:07:20-08:00","id":36075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=35862#post35862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sun Wukong says &quot;Na-a-aw&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless you really want to call the Great Sage Equaling Heaven a &quot;lesser&quot; anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am unaware of any myth in which Sun Wukong is born from the union of a God and a nymph/comparable Chinese mythological being. Chinese mythology is not my speciality, but was he not born of egg that was born of a rock? If anything he sounds like a Titanspawn that later converts to Godhood. So I'm not seeing how The Great Sage Equalling Heaven invalidates Telgar's point in any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:14:02-08:00","id":36079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=36075#post36075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am unaware of any myth in which Sun Wukong is born from the union of a God and a nymph/comparable Chinese mythological being. Chinese mythology is not my speciality, but was he not born of egg that was born of a rock? If anything he sounds like a Titanspawn that later converts to Godhood. So I'm not seeing how The Great Sage Equalling Heaven invalidates Telgar's point in any way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't calling Sun Wukong a Scion. I was laughing at the notion of that particular non-Scion being called a &quot;Lesser Immortal&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I just wanted to use the N-a-aw pun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 12-24-2013, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:27:49-08:00","id":36088,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you got to use your pun, but I never suggested that Sun Wukong was a &quot;Lesser Immortal&quot;. Not all Gods are born as Scions. In fact, most are not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:31:09-08:00","id":36091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=36079#post36079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't calling Sun Wukong a Scion. I was laughing at the notion of that particular non-Scion being called a &quot;Lesser Immortal&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I just wanted to use the N-a-aw pun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sun Wukong should definitely be a God. So, by the way, should Hermes, who IS born of a God/Nymph combo. I sometimes feel like Scion 1e gave off too much of a 'only Scions can become Gods' vibe. I still don't think we need those other routes to be playable, but a caveat to the effect that other routes exist would be nicely in keeping with mythology.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oops, typed in before I saw Telgar's reply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 12-24-2013, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:42:30-08:00","id":36106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=36088#post36088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad you got to use your pun, but I never suggested that Sun Wukong was a &quot;Lesser Immortal&quot;. Not all Gods are born as Scions. In fact, most are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>So why would the offspring of a deity and a non-Human be considered lesser than one of a deity and a human?<br /> And why shouldn't a game about those gods not have rules for a non-Scion become a god? Given it's such a common occurrence and all.<br /> <br /> Being that both are &quot;Children of the Gods.&quot;<br /> <br /> Samudra: And Loki, who was the Son of a Pair of Ice Giants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:47:40-08:00","id":36109,"title":"","content":"They're not &quot;less&quot;, but they're not Scions. They can be Gods, Immortals or whatever it is they are. But they cannot be Scions and, generally, are locked into whatever Legend zone they started off in. The ability to progress from near-mortal to Godhood is uniquely Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:56:10-08:00","id":36168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=35928#post35928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The further you get from Western Culture, the less myths fit into Scion's boxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But the number of myths that can be fit into Scion\u2019s boxes could be vastly increased with the inclusion of only a few new boxes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T00:11:42-08:00","id":36211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I could see human+nymph, like Achilles, but God+Elf would (should) be a Lesser Immortal, not a Scion. Scions need that spark of humanity to be super-special-awesome.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>As an opposing viewpoint, I have run several games where one or two characters were the children of two gods, or the children of a god and a non-human race. Generally it works out just fine and you can tell some great stories about it, and even get some interesting mileage from adding another dimension to the already turbulent culture clash that Scion tends to evoke. I personally do not find humanity to be particularly special, but I know I am in the minority on that issue. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T00:32:34-08:00","id":36216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=36211#post36211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an opposing viewpoint, I have run several games where one or two characters were the children of two gods, or the children of a god and a non-human race. Generally it works out just fine and you can tell some great stories about it, and even get some interesting mileage from adding another dimension to the already turbulent culture clash that Scion tends to evoke. I personally do not find humanity to be particularly special, but I know I am in the minority on that issue. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is mainly a difference in definitions. You could totally play as a Ghoul in a Vampire game and tell amazing stories and have a lot of fun and still fit the general mythos of the game, but you'd be playing a <i>Ghoul </i>NOT a Vampire. Similarly, you could play the characters you describe, but they wouldn't be <i>Scions.</i> They'd be something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T02:17:37-08:00","id":36251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=36216#post36216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this is mainly a difference in definitions. You could totally play as a Ghoul in a Vampire game and tell amazing stories and have a lot of fun and still fit the general mythos of the game, but you'd be playing a <i>Ghoul </i>NOT a Vampire. Similarly, you could play the characters you describe, but they wouldn't be <i>Scions.</i> They'd be something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I both agree and disagree with you! I agree in the sense that someone could tell a rocking story about being a Sidhe (and nothing but a Sidhe) going on adventures and eventually attaining apotheosis. But I also disagree in the sense that I think a Sidhe + God could create a Scion.<br /> <br /> That's speaking mechanically, of course. Different cultures could have all kinds of specific nomenclature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T08:11:13-08:00","id":36381,"title":"","content":"Just in the interest of expanding this line of discussion a bit?<br /> <br /> My only female player recently asked me about the prospect of creating a Scion who is the product of a God and an Amazon. What do you all think about this?<br /> <br /> It certainly makes sense mythologically. In fact, pretty much every Amazon who appears in Greek Mythology is, in fact, a daughter of Ares. So it's not like anyone can say that there's no grounds for it.<br /> <br /> .......And if any of you are following DC Comic's New 52? Yes, I'm sure she's drawing inspiration from Wonder Woman's new origin story. For those of you who don't know about Wonder Woman's new origin: she is now the daughter of Queen Hippolyta of the Amazons (as always) and Zeus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T08:47:01-08:00","id":36398,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. Amazons are pretty much mortal. They may have the blood of Ares in them, but I don't think he's ever visited any of them, and even if he did, none of them ever made it to Godhood. The union should result in a textbook Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T09:15:40-08:00","id":36408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=36398#post36398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why not. Amazons are pretty much mortal. They may have the blood of Ares in them, but I don't think he's ever visited any of them, and even if he did, none of them ever made it to Godhood. The union should result in a textbook Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my thinking as well.<br /> <br /> The only thing that gives me pause is that business where Amazons pretty much get maxed out Physical Attributes and even maxed out Appearance at character creation. A character that starts out with that many maxed out Attributes might disrupt character creation a bit.<br /> <br /> I suppose I could just suspend that rule and have her design the character as normal and have her just concentrate on her Physicals and Appearance when prioritizing her dot allocation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T09:25:34-08:00","id":36417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=36408#post36408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only thing that gives me pause is that business where Amazons pretty much get maxed out Physical Attributes and even maxed out Appearance at character creation. A character that starts out with that many maxed out Attributes might disrupt character creation a bit.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Where is that rule from? I do not remember reading it, but it has been a long time. If you are referring to the tendency of Amazons to have those stats maxed, that is really just representative of their culture. Also, Amazons traditionally have children with males of other cultures - <i>mortal </i>males. The child of a God and an Amazon is a different kettle of fish altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T09:39:11-08:00","id":36428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=36408#post36408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is my thinking as well.<br /> <br /> The only thing that gives me pause is that business where Amazons pretty much get maxed out Physical Attributes and even maxed out Appearance at character creation. A character that starts out with that many maxed out Attributes might disrupt character creation a bit.<br /> <br /> I suppose I could just suspend that rule and have her design the character as normal and have her just concentrate on her Physicals and Appearance when prioritizing her dot allocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am of the opinion that when a character wants something powerful, they should usually get it, but with significant drawbacks to balance it out. For example, rather than simply saying that this Amazon Scion is just like a normal Scion mechanically, go ahead and give them, say, an extra dot in appearance and one or 2 extra dots to put into physicals. Then give them some drawbacks for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T10:39:33-08:00","id":36441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=36417#post36417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where is that rule from? I do not remember reading it, but it has been a long time. If you are referring to the tendency of Amazons to have those stats maxed, that is really just representative of their culture. Also, Amazons traditionally have children with males of other cultures - <i>mortal </i>males. The child of a God and an Amazon is a different kettle of fish altogether.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm pretty sure that the Amazon write-up in Hero says that the &quot;Amazon Template&quot; involves all the Physicals at 5 dots and Appearance at 5 dots just kind of as a default.<br /> <br /> The write-up also says that the Amazons always try to acquire male Scions for breeding purposes because the child of an Amazon and a Scion gets even BETTER Attribute upgrades commensurate with the Scion's Legend rating. Thus, Amazons aren't exactly fully human and things may be a little different for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T10:41:30-08:00","id":36444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=36428#post36428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am of the opinion that when a character wants something powerful, they should usually get it, but with significant drawbacks to balance it out. For example, rather than simply saying that this Amazon Scion is just like a normal Scion mechanically, go ahead and give them, say, an extra dot in appearance and one or 2 extra dots to put into physicals. Then give them some drawbacks for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of drawbacks are you thinking?<br /> <br /> Maybe a dot penalty in her other Attributes? Like &quot;Okay you can have another three dots for your Physicals, but you'll have to give up three of your Mental dots&quot; or something? Or maybe something a little more esoteric? Like a derangement or some other classic White Wolf Flaw?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T10:44:42-08:00","id":36445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=36444#post36444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What kind of drawbacks are you thinking?<br /> <br /> Maybe a dot penalty in her other Attributes? Like &quot;Okay you can have another three dots for your Physicals, but you'll have to give up three of your Mental dots&quot; or something? Or maybe something a little more esoteric? Like a derangement or some other classic White Wolf Flaw?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go the more esoteric route, partly because it makes for more interesting roleplay and isn't just &quot;oh spend some XP here to shore up your weakness&quot;. Potential example might be penalty to non-Appearance-based social interaction roles when dealing with males, due to lack of experience in an Amazon upbringing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T10:51:51-08:00","id":36451,"title":"","content":"I checked the book. Amazons start with Physicals at 2 each and Appearance at 3. My suggestion would be to treat it the way nWOD treats having supernatural templates, where each character may only have one template at a time, losing all advantages of one if they take on another. Your Amazon Scion will be the peak of human perfection, so long as she remains untapped by her divine father, but the moment he Visits her, I suggest that she lose her Amazon privileges. She's not an Amazon any more after all, no matter how much she denies it.<br /> <br /> Of course, that is going by the template. My personal preference would be to scrap that. Amazons in mythology are simply human women at the peak of physical conditioning. Making their strength supernatural is, in my opinion, cheapening their achievements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T11:34:36-08:00","id":36476,"title":"","content":"As a long-time Champions player, my preference is to say that character background has no mechanical impact on character creation. (Champions is a point-based system: You spend X number of points on Characteristics, Skills, Powers, etc. and whether you justify the character's superhumanity on being a mutant, a mythological god, a highly trained person or, heck, the highly trained offspring of a mutant and a mythological god makes no difference in the number of points you recieve.) Scions already have higher numbers of Attribute dots than normal humans. Whether you say it's just because of the divine heritage or from being part Amazon is window dressing. <br /> <br /> I think it's important that players are all following the same rules when they make up their characters. Creating special exceptions for particular backstories opens a can of worms that I at least would prefer to avoid. <br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T17:16:44-08:00","id":36634,"title":"","content":"If she wants high Physical stats, she should pay for them, Amazon or no. Citing a special upbringing is no good - all PCs, by definition, have a special upbringing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T06:46:39-08:00","id":36901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=36451#post36451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I checked the book. Amazons start with Physicals at 2 each and Appearance at 3. My suggestion would be to treat it the way nWOD treats having supernatural templates, where each character may only have one template at a time, losing all advantages of one if they take on another. Your Amazon Scion will be the peak of human perfection, so long as she remains untapped by her divine father, but the moment he Visits her, I suggest that she lose her Amazon privileges. She's not an Amazon any more after all, no matter how much she denies it.<br /> <br /> Of course, that is going by the template. My personal preference would be to scrap that. Amazons in mythology are simply human women at the peak of physical conditioning. Making their strength supernatural is, in my opinion, cheapening their achievements.</div> </div> </div> </div>????<br /> <br /> I have the book in my hands right now.<br /> <br /> &quot;The characteristics of an amazon are identical to those of an experienced soldier save that the amazon is invariably female and begins with one extra dot in Strength, Dexterity and Stamina, as well as two extra dots in Appearance.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, the stats of an experienced soldier are Strength 4 Stamina 4 Dexterity 4 and Appearance 3. One dot extra in the Physicals equals five across the board. Two extra dots of Appearance raises it to 5.<br /> <br /> I'm torn on the issue of &quot;supernatural vs peak human&quot; Amazons stuff. On the one hand? Yes, saying they're peak humans through conditioning and training solves the character creation problem. On the other hand, there's no way to explain how they're all super-hot. Then they have two other supernatural elements to them. First? They only give birth to daughters. Yes, you could eliminate that as well, I suppose. But then you're into New 52 DC Amazons territory where they kill or sell their male babies into slavery. Second supernatural trait? They have Virtues. Normal humans don't.<br /> <br /> It seems pretty clear the Amazons are intended to be at least somewhat supernatural to me. Not sure how to go about changing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T06:57:52-08:00","id":36903,"title":"","content":"Oops, applied the extra dots as free ones on the character sheet before you allocate points. Sorry, I clearly started celebrating Christmas too early.<br /> <br /> In that case, I suggest the nWOD solution. Remove the effects of the Amazon template the moment she is Visited (because it really isn't fair on the other players).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T09:05:13-08:00","id":36934,"title":"","content":"Those antagonist stats are to represent fully trained Amazons, not <i>every single Amazon ever</i>. It's totally possible to have ugly Amazons, or ones without 5/5/5 physicals. The book is just giving basic guidelines for a generic Amazon Follower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T11:01:41-08:00","id":36969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=36934#post36934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those antagonist stats are to represent fully trained Amazons, not <i>every single Amazon ever</i>. It's totally possible to have ugly Amazons, or ones without 5/5/5 physicals. The book is just giving basic guidelines for a generic Amazon Follower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Come to think of it, you're probably right. Yeah, they didn't exactly have the page space to drive home that point. But the Amazons are presented as either antagonists or Followers, so of COURSE they'd have to &quot;generic&quot; them up some.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I think I'll just tell my player to build a character as normal. I may let her have one or two free dots just because she's a really great player and a team player who always thinks about other people in the group first.<br /> <br /> I should clarify that this player of mine didn't just walk up to me and say &quot;I want to be an Amazon, so I can have maxed out stats for free.&quot; She came to me and said &quot;I've got an idea for an Amazon Scion, but how do we get around those maxed out stats?&quot; She was asking about this in the specific hope that she could build this character WITHOUT making everyone else look like a chump.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I guess I'll let her go ahead with the design and if she thinks she could REALLY use just one or two extra dots, I may just let her have them.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the advice, guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T08:06:58-08:00","id":37323,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s also worth noting that Scion 1e didn\u2019t have anything like <b>Scion: Origins</b>, which meant that the <i>weakest</i> mythological beings were tuned to work with or against Heroes. In <b>Scion 2e</b>, a case could be made that some of the Followers, Guides, and antagonists from 1e\u2019s <b>Scion: Hero</b> ought to be downgraded to the level of <b>Origins</b>, possibly with the ability to upgrade individuals in their ranks to a level comparable to Heroes. I could definitely see doing this with Amazons, with some of them having no Legend and others having as much as Legend \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (plus Epic physicals and/or Epic Appearance, assuming 2e still has Appearance).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T19:47:02-08:00","id":37625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=37323#post37323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">assuming 2e still has Appearance</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been forever and a half so this very well may be outdated, but I seem to vaguely recall some quote out there saying that they were gonna stick with Appearance, because it was an easier attribute to make powers from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/93-xegek","name":"Xegek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar93_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T04:02:13-08:00","id":37782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xegek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=37625#post37625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's been forever and a half so this very well may be outdated, but I seem to vaguely recall some quote out there saying that they were gonna stick with Appearance, because it was an easier attribute to make powers from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that there have been statements to that effect for Exalted. I don't recall anything along those lines for Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T05:13:56-08:00","id":37796,"title":"","content":"I hope they do keep it. Not only are Appearance based powers a critical part of the mythic landscape (Aphrodite would probably commit suicide without them), I cannot for the life of me think of a God who has Epic Composure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T06:13:20-08:00","id":37820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=35928#post35928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The further you get from Western Culture, the less myths fit into Scion's boxes.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's a thing that we have noticed, yes. It's also worth noting that the first edition rarely followed its own fluff on the matter, and an early developmental shift muddied the issue. You can see the shift happen smack dab in the middle of the corebook: it starts off by talking about how not everything fits into the classification of God or Titan and then proceeds to classify literally everything into those boxes (even poor Simurgh). Ghosts are about the closest thing you have to a neutral entity. There is some talk of how to classify Loki or Aphrodite based on descent from a Titan, too, and how they were in one box but not the other. It's all Titans or Gods after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T06:59:14-08:00","id":37833,"title":"","content":"There's much that I see in various pantheons that don't come across as a fair presentation of this or that deity/titan. Which is why I'd rewrite some things and allow certain titans and titanspawn to be accessible. And certain deities that were/are evil, should be seen as that. If a follower of Prometheus is trying to stop a scion that is conducting a ritual involving human sacrifice, I should think a reasonable response would be to the benefit of Prometheus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T09:28:43-08:00","id":37897,"title":"","content":"The hardest part is that which is divine but not a god. China's legends and mythology are riddled with these kinds of figures. I'm not sure this is necessarily something the game needs to do more than simply acknowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T12:12:03-08:00","id":37952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue Ryong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=37782#post37782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that there have been statements to that effect for Exalted. I don't recall anything along those lines for Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. I checked the Exalted 3E spoilers wiki and it was something said about Lunar charms. But I personally hope they keep Appearance for the exact same reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/93-xegek","name":"Xegek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar93_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T15:57:33-08:00","id":38045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=37897#post37897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hardest part is that which is divine but not a god. China's legends and mythology are riddled with these kinds of figures. I'm not sure this is necessarily something the game needs to do more than simply acknowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would this mean in game terms? In particular, what do you mean by \u201cdivine, but not a god\u201d, both concept-wise and system-wise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T01:19:52-08:00","id":38200,"title":"","content":"China has quite a few beings who were elevated to immortality but are neither gods nor godborns in mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T01:45:09-08:00","id":38204,"title":"","content":"&quot;Little Gods&quot; and such. There's not a good English language equivalent or matching category. Basically, they're Legend 2-8 figures that would, in Scion terms, be Lesser Immortals or Titanspawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T04:39:54-08:00","id":38246,"title":"","content":"The issue of little gods is almost entirely one of definition and not one of mechanics. They are not at the power level of 'gods', and probably would not be classified as 'gods' by our definition, but they are certainly classified as 'gods' in the definition of their own culture. In front of the curtain we can continue to call them gods, while behind the curtain the mechanics of the game can classify them as whatever they need to be classified as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T05:24:13-08:00","id":38252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=38045#post38045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would this mean in game terms? In particular, what do you mean by \u201cdivine, but not a god\u201d, both concept-wise and system-wise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Telgar said, it doesn't translate. Not even sloppily. They sort of fill the same role as Greek demigods did; going out, undertaking the quests, moving the pieces around the board to help save the world. Although quite a few are simply mentioned once and then never again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T07:11:39-08:00","id":38278,"title":"","content":"Field agents of the gods, at least sometimes.<br /> <br /> They're kinda all around the world in some ways. bodhisattva, the eight immortals, bogatyrs (?), The Catholic saints might even fit in assuming there's room for the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T07:50:43-08:00","id":38290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=38246#post38246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue of little gods is almost entirely one of definition and not one of mechanics. They are not at the power level of 'gods', and probably would not be classified as 'gods' by our definition, but they are certainly classified as 'gods' in the definition of their own culture. In front of the curtain we can continue to call them gods, while behind the curtain the mechanics of the game can classify them as whatever they need to be classified as.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a pseudo aequivalent though also in another religion: kamis of japanese religion (although those are born immortal already while those in china are born mortal)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T09:20:05-08:00","id":38303,"title":"","content":"I'm not seeing the problem with categorizing minor shen as lesser immortals. Some shen are born of other shen, some shen are converted Titanspawn, some shen are mortals who became lesser immortals while living, while some shen are mortals who became lesser immortals upon death because of sufficient enlightenment.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd prefer a blurring of the line between gods and lesser immortals because the barrier seems like an artificial distinction to me. An awful lot of nymphs were born of godly unions, while Idunn is supposed to be descended from Ivaldi. Furthermore, I think it might be interesting if the children of unions between mortals and lesser mortals resulted in people with supernatural inclinations, though much less so than Scions. For example, Zeus and Alcmene produces Heracles, but the child of Kuzunoha is Abe no Seimei.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T03:40:18-08:00","id":38665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=38290#post38290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a pseudo aequivalent though also in another religion: kamis of japanese religion (although those are born immortal already while those in china are born mortal)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite right. Kami means God in Japanese actually. Same thing for Shen.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I just read what those new books will be about and I feel horrible: I don't want to play Scion until the new books are out because I would have to replay Scion all over again and I'm really not sure whether my players would agree... At the same time, I don't know how to stop playing it... <br /> By the way, any release date that has been written anywhere? Sorry if I'm making anyone repeat it... Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T07:35:59-08:00","id":38725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=38665#post38665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite right. Kami means God in Japanese actually. Same thing for Shen.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I just read what those new books will be about and I feel horrible: I don't want to play Scion until the new books are out because I would have to replay Scion all over again and I'm really not sure whether my players would agree... At the same time, I don't know how to stop playing it...<br /> By the way, any release date that has been written anywhere? Sorry if I'm making anyone repeat it... Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/\" target=\"_blank\">According to the schedule</a>, May 2014, but keep in mind that's only an estimate and likely to slip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T10:05:18-08:00","id":38777,"title":"","content":"Oh, next year. I thought it would be much later than that. Thank you<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T19:12:55-08:00","id":41457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=38200#post38200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">China has quite a few beings who were elevated to immortality but are neither gods nor godborns in mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's the term &quot;god&quot; that is the problem, really. Modern English-speakers bring a lot of Christianizing assumptions along with the word. But really all it means is &quot;something that receives worship,&quot; and that's not an essential category. In ancient Greece, a <i>theos</i> could be anything from a powerful cosmic spirit to a local protective spirit to a dead ancestor to a living monarch. You could be born a mortal and become a <i>theos </i>if and when people in your region started treating you as a god (i.e. offering sacrifice and votive offerings in return for your aid). Chinese practice isn't significantly different, nor is Japanese, ancient Mesopotamian, or pretty much any other traditional culture whose concept of divinity hasn't been influenced by Christianity.<br /> <br /> Scion adds an additional wrinkle in positing that gods are a particular species of being, distinct from powerful mortals, ghosts, heroes, et al., and mortals' attitude towards them is only part of the picture of how they got to be that way. So in Scion, the <i>Theoi</i> and the <i>Shen</i> are more specific than just any beings who receive divine worship; they're extended families whose status is hereditary and tied to the ichor in their veins. Of course, in ancient Greek (and quite possibly Chinese) myth, it's no problem, since everybody with a name has divine ancestry somewhere in their family tree. So it's easy to show how heroes like Heracles and Diomedes become gods. Does the same apply to Guan Yu? Not sure, but in any case every culture with gods has myths about mortals who were elevated to their ranks. Were they Scions? Maybe. Or maybe there are other means besides genetics by which a mortal can acquire a Legend rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T00:08:07-08:00","id":47277,"title":"","content":"I'm really curious to see how Scion's going to work. I enjoyed the first edition, though the group started hitting a wall around Demigod level, heading into God. We wanted to try to customize our abilities to match how we saw our characters progressing, and were uncertain how to go about this - one character wanted to go more dryad, but couldn't find many powers that would fit her command of plants, for example.<br /> <br /> I'm also definitely interested in seeing how the gods of Japan are done. The Amatsukami are cool, but I'm also hoping to see the Kunitsukami as well. I'm Shinto, so I'm very interested in seeing how my faith is laid out in 2nd Edition. The term we use for the pantheon of Japan (some eight million gods) is the &quot;Yaoyorozu-no-Kami&quot;, which effectively means &quot;Everything&quot;. If we're focussing on the divine gods of Heaven and Earth, we use &quot;Tenjinchigi&quot;. I played a Greek scion myself, but my sister really dug into the Japanese pantheon (and made a scion of Ame no Uzume no Mikoto). I'm sure she'll want to play that character again, and it would be interesting if the new book goes closer to her expectations, or further away.<br /> <br /> I think the only real beef I had with it was the idea that every god, in every pantheon, practiced adultery. This kind of rubbed me the wrong way - sure the Greek pantheon was known for this, but every pantheon? (My sister points out there's no indication that Ame no Uzume no Mikoto betrayed her husband, for example).<br /> <br /> Still, looking forward to this, and if I need to, I'll tweak the game for when I'm running it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T00:58:53-08:00","id":47288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tashiro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=47277#post47277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the only real beef I had with it was the idea that every god, in every pantheon, practiced adultery. This kind of rubbed me the wrong way - sure the Greek pantheon was known for this, but every pantheon? (My sister points out there's no indication that Ame no Uzume no Mikoto betrayed her husband, for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>There is actually a whole sidebar in Companion, in the chapter regarding the Deva (another famously monogamous Pantheon) with alternatives for such cases. As such, the simplest explanation - adoption, is presented in the corebook itself. Amaterasu and Tsuki-yomi are divorced, and thus free to have children. Inari is a fertility deity and thus likely to have more than enough children to go around, and there are eight million minor Kami whose children can all be adopted by the distinguished personages in Takamagahara. I think that might be the best route for your sister. I mean, half the Hindu Pantheon is probably dependant entirely on Indra's loins for their Scions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T01:16:22-08:00","id":47291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=47288#post47288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is actually a whole sidebar in Companion, in the chapter regarding the Deva (another famously monogamous Pantheon) with alternatives for such cases. As such, the simplest explanation - adoption, is presented in the corebook itself. Amaterasu and Tsuki-yomi are divorced, and thus free to have children. Inari is a fertility deity and thus likely to have more than enough children to go around, and there are eight million minor Kami whose children can all be adopted by the distinguished personages in Takamagahara. I think that might be the best route for your sister. I mean, half the Hindu Pantheon is probably dependant entirely on Indra's loins for their Scions.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall Amaterasu and Tsuki-yomi are siblings and not the married kind. I think in many ways they are treated as twins. Coming from Izangi's eyes and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T04:33:30-08:00","id":47323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=47291#post47291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I recall Amaterasu and Tsuki-yomi are siblings and not the married kind. I think in many ways they are treated as twins. Coming from Izangi's eyes and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they're always siblings, and triplets, along with Susanoo. The version I read has them as married and then divorced after the Uke-Mochi debacle. Of course, this being mythology, and a still living one with a mostly unbroken history at that, I do not doubt that there is another version where they're not married. I seem to remember there is another version of the Uke-Mochi myth where Susanoo does the deed.<br /> <br /> Either way, the point stands, Amaterasu and Tsuki-Yomi are free to have extra children for their monogamous colleagues. Unless you want to bring Takami-Musubi into the picture. And that guy's so obscure and remote he's always struck me as a Titan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T13:01:27-08:00","id":47571,"title":"","content":"Izanagi-no-Mikoto and Izanami-no-Mikoto are brother and sister, <i>and </i>husband and wife. Amaterasu Omikami and Tsukiyomi no Mikoto are also husband and wife, sister and brother. They never divorced, but did have children over time (which is where the Imperial line comes from). And while Uke-Mochi was killed, there's some indication she simply reincarnated (as O-Inari) - or she may have been O-Inari's wife - the jury's still out on this.<br /> <br /> I'm doing historical research on O-Inari, which means I've had a good hard look at the Japanese pantheon. Susano-O caused a huge fuss with Amateras Omikami by throwing a horse's hide into her sewing room, causing her daughter / sister (jury's out on that one) to freak out and kill herself. Strangely, <i>that</i> individual is also considered an aspect of O-Inari. Then again, so is Izanagi no Mikoto and Izanami no Mikoto. And Amaterasu Omikami's grandson, who brought the three sacred treasures to the first Emperor of Japan. So, O-Inari is Amaterasu Omikami's parents, sister/daughter, and grandson. Oh, and three of the Seven Fortunes (Daikoku, Benten, and Benzaiten), and also the Ame no Uzume no Mikoto, who danced to draw Amaterasu Omikami out of her cave, <i>and </i>her husband Sarutahiko Okami.<br /> <br /> The thing is, Shinto is... interesting. <b>Anything</b> which inspires wonder or joy is a kami. And anything that is a kami can be revered. And if it is has a form, it is also a god. Going by the Shinto tradition, the Monkey King (while being a character from a known work of fiction) is an actual god, and respected as such. But this goes for any character as well. In fact, the Japanese have a word for 'gods of other lands', and these gods are respected and revered as kami. This is how they incorporated Hindu, Chinese, and Buddhist gods into the pantheon, and goes far beyond that. Jesus Christ? Yes, he's a kami. So are all the Archangels, named Angels, and Saints. They're all 'equivalent' as far as divine prestige is concerned.<br /> <br /> And it gets a bit mind-breaking as well - fictional characters are considered fair game (as per the Monkey King). This means Sherlock Holmes, Santa Claus, Harry Potter, and any other character who is inspirational can be accepted as a kami. You hear of Japanese men marrying their virtual idols? Well, that's because these virtual idols are <i>kami</i>, and as <i>kami</i>, they exist as beings. The Japanese pantheon has an endless supply of kami to call upon when needed... through the entertainment industry, they can produce hundreds of thousands of kami to throw onto the front lines, and the larger the fan-base, the more powerful the kami can probably become.<br /> <br /> The thing with O-Inari is that she's a composite goddess. The 'five gods who make one' thing isn't unique to her either, but in Shinto, it is understood that these individual gods are individual gods, but also O-Inari, and O-Inari is her own being, and also these individual gods. I can understand the concept, having taken years to wrap my head around Shinto before I joined the faith, but it falls neatly into the 'if it inspires, it exists'. O-Inari is the most famous god in Japan, with over a million shrines. When I asked my Sensei about this, whether O-Inari is an individual or a group, and whether it was right to revere her as an individual or as part of a whole, he answered 'yes'. To his mind, these are not contradictions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm probably going to stick with my Greek demigod, but I'm certain my sister's going to want to delve back into the Japanese pantheon, and she's going to want to try to adhere to the Shinto faith as close as she can - her character is a shrine maiden after all (and her mother, Ame-no-Uzume-no-Mikoto, was the <i>first </i>shrine maiden).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T13:44:46-08:00","id":47586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tashiro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=47571#post47571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with O-Inari is that she's a composite goddess. The 'five gods who make one' thing isn't unique to her either, but in Shinto, it is understood that these individual gods are individual gods, but also O-Inari, and O-Inari is her own being, and also these individual gods. I can understand the concept, having taken years to wrap my head around Shinto before I joined the faith, but it falls neatly into the 'if it inspires, it exists'. O-Inari is the most famous god in Japan, with over a million shrines. When I asked my Sensei about this, whether O-Inari is an individual or a group, and whether it was right to revere her as an individual or as part of a whole, he answered 'yes'. To his mind, these are not contradictions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think I understand the concept, since it is very similar to Hinduism's concept of Nirguna Brahman. The parallels between our religions is fascinating.<br /> <br /> Your explanation of the generation of new Kami makes Tsukumo-Gami sound a lot more interesting. It sounds not entirely unlike how many Hindu villages and various sacred groves have lesser immortal guardians or the nymphs of Greek myth, only far more widely applicable. Tell me, would you consider these spontaneously generated kami to be lesser immortals or minor Legend 9 Gods? I know Tsukumo-Gami does the former (and honestly, I prefer it that way), but I would like an actual Shinto perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 01-12-2014, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T14:28:26-08:00","id":47611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=47586#post47586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I understand the concept, since it is very similar to Hinduism's concept of Nirguna Brahman. The parallels between our religions is fascinating.<br /> <br /> Your explanation of the generation of new Kami makes Tsukumo-Gami sound a lot more interesting. It sounds not entirely unlike how many Hindu villages and various sacred groves have lesser immortal guardians or the nymphs of Greek myth, only far more widely applicable. Tell me, would you consider these spontaneously generated kami to be lesser immortals or minor Legend 9 Gods? I know Tsukumo-Gami does the former (and honestly, I prefer it that way), but I would like an actual Shinto perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would really depend on the portfolio of the kami in question. If it is a kami of a lesser grove or something, it would probably be appropriate to say 'Demigod'. The other thing to consider is whether it is an embodied kami or a disembodied spirit. The latter are not venerated directly, though they're still powerful spirits. 'The spirit of the forest' is considered a being, but not a god, but the moment it takes a host and manifests an avatar, it is considered to be a god. Once it leaves again, it becomes 'the spirit'.<br /> <br /> The local museum had a Vodou exhibit, which was an incredible experience. One of the things which astonished me was that Vodou and Shinto are damn near sibling religions. They have kami, they have ancestors, they have the goal of &quot;community over the self&quot; - the happiness of those around you is worth more than your personal desires (and in turn, your community is expected to put your happiness over their desires as well). The idea of voodoo dolls is complete and utter bullcrap in the Vodou faith, and is <b>not a thing</b>.<br /> <br /> The entire thing was eye-opening, and I was able to understand the concepts presented for Vodou clearly, having spent so much time studying Shinto. It is a very ... clean.. religion, in that sense. The other thing that Shinto and Vodou have in common is the idea that &quot;good&quot; and &quot;evil&quot; are not spiritual concepts - neither religion has anything to do with the cosmic battle of Good vs Evil, because these things <b>do not exist</b>. &quot;Evil&quot; is defined by humanity and human laws. It is defined as 'what harms the community'. What Shinto, and Vodou, focus on is <b>spiritual purity</b>. That is why these faiths focus on ritual purification. They want your spirit and body to be unsullied by negativity and unclean things.<br /> <br /> And from the perspective of Shinto, all spirits are innately pure. They are not Good or Evil, they simply exist in accordance to their nature. A spirit, within its natural habitat, exists in harmony with that habitat. If it is moved outside of its habitat, then you get disharmony. The spirit acts purely in accordance with its nature, but the environment may not be meant for it. So the goal is to appease the spirit, bring it where it should be, and all will be well. Or, as an example: A demon in the Chinese Hells tortures sinners, cleansing them of their sins before the soul can reincarnate. That's well and good. The demon isn't <b>evil</b>, it is fulfilling its purpose. Summon the demon to Earth, and what do you get? A demon surrounded by people who are still filled with sin. So the demon tortures and wounds these people trying to purify them. Of course, these people still have fleshy bodies, so .. they die and suffer. The demon senses this suffering, and does more, trying to &quot;correct&quot; this as it only knows how. This is imbalanced, and so exorcism sends the demon back to Hell, where it can return to doing its job. The demon isn't evil.<br /> <br /> Of course, from a human perspective, the demon is evil, since it is torturing and killing. But that isn't the demon's fault - it is in the wrong place. So to deal with the demon, you should remain respectful and courteous, and then send it the hell on its way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T09:23:06-08:00","id":49854,"title":"","content":"Hello, all. Just wanted to drop in with some slightly more solid information on Scion: Origins, though Neall has graciously touched base on some of this.<br /> <br /> I've got several goals with this book. This stuff is from my outline for the book, as an aside. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Rules Book:</b> First and foremost, I wanted a book where we can consolidate the majority of the system. Doing so gives us extra room in the Hero through God books for richer background material.<br /> <br /> <b>Pre-Visitation Scions:</b> There's plenty of indication that Scions are just flat-out exceptional in many ways even before they receive that Visitation that brings them to awareness of their own semi-divine nature. For some folks, it's enough to just handwave and narrate away those sorts of stories, but if there is a motto I have as a developer, it is: &quot;I like options.&quot; I love running prelude arcs, and know plenty of other folks do as well, so we'll be including some mechanics for these just-above-normal mortals, and give some guidelines for running Visitations and the like.<br /> <br /> <b>Followers:</b> This is also where we're going to include the mechanics for presenting the various not-quite-divine sorts of characters that were often Birthrights in Scion1e: Amazons, satyrs, and that crew. These mechanics will provide stats for those characters to be used as NPCs or as player characters. We'll also be including some mechanics in Hero for granting these entities a full dot of Legend and &quot;leveling them up&quot; so that your Demigod can possibly have Hero-level cohorts and leave them in the dust once he transcends to demigodhood, or so players who want to play such a character in an otherwise Hero-level campaign may do so.<br /> <br /> <b>Mortals &amp; the Fated:</b> While the full rules for Fatebinding and the like are in Hero, Origins will be what you use to create those characters that become tied to your Scions. It's essentially a &quot;mortals rulebook,&quot; with the options of adding some templates to them to turn them into supernatural creatures (though we aren't specifically using the &quot;template&quot; mechanic for this).<br /> <br /> <b>Sorcerers, Priests &amp; Oracles:</b> This book will also include rules for reflecting those mortals whose lives have been touched by Legend in some capacity. They might be occultists and spiritualists who are Getting It Right, they might be oracles and seers haunted by divine vision, they might be those who still render up worship in the Old Ways (or Current Ways for some!). These folks will also get some &quot;level up&quot; potential that follower/cohort-types do in Hero.<br /> <br /> <b>Antagonists:</b> There were plenty of not-quite-Hero-scale antagonists in the original game, many of them supernatural gribblies: vampires, ghosts, werewolves. This is going to be where those get placed, as well - also not just as NPCs, and with the potential to &quot;level up&quot; to Hero-scale so you can have awesome ancient vampire lords, super-werewolves and whatnot.<br /> <br /> <b>Urban Fantasy:</b> Because I don't like the idea of a core rulebook that just &quot;serves&quot; another sort of game entirely, we're also making this book a sort of &quot;urban fantasy RPG,&quot; as it were. Inspired by stories as myriad as Butcher's Dresden to the works of Charles de Lint and everything inbetween (and beyond), we'd like this game to provide some inspiration for the sorts of stories you might tell about a world that has seen an upswing in Legend once more and how that affects normal folks.<br /> <br /> So, yes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There you have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Regards,<br /> Joseph D. Carriker<br /> -------------------------------------------<br /> \u201cIn Springtime, O Dionysos, To thy holy temple come,<br /> To Elis with thy Graces, Rushing with thy bull-foot, come,<br /> Noble Bull, Noble Bull\u201d<br /> \u2015 Plutarch","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1242-jdcarriker","name":"JDCarriker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T09:47:05-08:00","id":49863,"title":"","content":"Oh now that sounds like all kinds of awesome.<br /> <br /> One of my favourite parts of Scion 1e was the idea that you're NOT hidden away by some masquerade or mandated secrecy but that you could very literally walk down the street, ablaze in golden glory as the Scion of the Sun God. Sure it caused trouble...but damn was it fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So the line about Urban Fantasy in a world with an upswing in Legend sounds great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T09:56:48-08:00","id":49870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JDCarriker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=49854#post49854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, all. Just wanted to drop in with some slightly more solid information on Scion: Origins, though Neall has graciously touched base on some of this.<br /> <br /> I've got several goals with this book. This stuff is from my outline for the book, as an aside. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Rules Book:</b> First and foremost, I wanted a book where we can consolidate the majority of the system. Doing so gives us extra room in the Hero through God books for richer background material.<br /> <br /> <b>Pre-Visitation Scions:</b> There's plenty of indication that Scions are just flat-out exceptional in many ways even before they receive that Visitation that brings them to awareness of their own semi-divine nature. For some folks, it's enough to just handwave and narrate away those sorts of stories, but if there is a motto I have as a developer, it is: &quot;I like options.&quot; I love running prelude arcs, and know plenty of other folks do as well, so we'll be including some mechanics for these just-above-normal mortals, and give some guidelines for running Visitations and the like.<br /> <br /> <b>Followers:</b> This is also where we're going to include the mechanics for presenting the various not-quite-divine sorts of characters that were often Birthrights in Scion1e: Amazons, satyrs, and that crew. These mechanics will provide stats for those characters to be used as NPCs or as player characters. We'll also be including some mechanics in Hero for granting these entities a full dot of Legend and &quot;leveling them up&quot; so that your Demigod can possibly have Hero-level cohorts and leave them in the dust once he transcends to demigodhood, or so players who want to play such a character in an otherwise Hero-level campaign may do so.<br /> <br /> <b>Mortals &amp; the Fated:</b> While the full rules for Fatebinding and the like are in Hero, Origins will be what you use to create those characters that become tied to your Scions. It's essentially a &quot;mortals rulebook,&quot; with the options of adding some templates to them to turn them into supernatural creatures (though we aren't specifically using the &quot;template&quot; mechanic for this).<br /> <br /> <b>Sorcerers, Priests &amp; Oracles:</b> This book will also include rules for reflecting those mortals whose lives have been touched by Legend in some capacity. They might be occultists and spiritualists who are Getting It Right, they might be oracles and seers haunted by divine vision, they might be those who still render up worship in the Old Ways (or Current Ways for some!). These folks will also get some &quot;level up&quot; potential that follower/cohort-types do in Hero.<br /> <br /> <b>Antagonists:</b> There were plenty of not-quite-Hero-scale antagonists in the original game, many of them supernatural gribblies: vampires, ghosts, werewolves. This is going to be where those get placed, as well - also not just as NPCs, and with the potential to &quot;level up&quot; to Hero-scale so you can have awesome ancient vampire lords, super-werewolves and whatnot.<br /> <br /> <b>Urban Fantasy:</b> Because I don't like the idea of a core rulebook that just &quot;serves&quot; another sort of game entirely, we're also making this book a sort of &quot;urban fantasy RPG,&quot; as it were. Inspired by stories as myriad as Butcher's Dresden to the works of Charles de Lint and everything inbetween (and beyond), we'd like this game to provide some inspiration for the sorts of stories you might tell about a world that has seen an upswing in Legend once more and how that affects normal folks.<br /> <br /> So, yes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There you have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every word of this post feeds my hunger for this game! Thank you very much for sharing, Mr. Carriker!<br /> <br /> 1.) I like the idea of concentrating the rules in a single book. Or at least the core rules. I'm sure there will be others in the Hero, Demigod, and God books.<br /> <br /> 2.) I was just thinking about Scions being exceptional even before their Visitation today. It only makes sense really. I mean, unless Zeus somehow Visited Heracles as a baby, how the Hell did he strangle those two serpents in his crib? Mortal babies can't do that. So how could Heracles have possibly done this before his Visitation? Sounds like your ideas might just explain this.<br /> <br /> 3.) I love the idea of upgrade-able Followers. I also love getting full stats for them so players will actually be able to see the benefits of taking Followers.<br /> <br /> 4.) Mortals &amp; the Fated intrigue me greatly. I'm all kinds of excited to see what you can do with this goodness. Seeing how Fate interacts with mortals will be intriguing and the option for turning them into supernatural creatures will likely add all kinds of depth to storytelling.<br /> <br /> 5.) Sorcerers, Priests &amp; Oracles is possibly the thing I'm most excited to see. While I do agree that Scions shouldn't have much to fear from mortals, it will be really nice to be able to come up with mortals who can at least somehow pose a challenge to Scions for a little while at least. Mortals don't have to be able to kill Scions, but it will be nice to see them having at least the potential to be somewhat relevant in the game. The fact that they can also be boon companions or genuinely helpful to Scions also makes them interesting. I can't wait to learn more about this one.<br /> <br /> 6.) Antagonists are always fun. Especially when they're upgrade-able. Very excited to see how to pit Scions against vampire lords and the like.<br /> <br /> 7.) Urban Fantasy sounds very cool. Seeing how the magical world comes back to this shitty, mundane world of ours will be awesome, and it'll make the world of Scion much deeper and more fun to explore.<br /> <br /> I can't wait to learn more. Keep up the good work, sir!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T11:06:59-08:00","id":49927,"title":"","content":"I cannot like your post enough! Thanks for the info and for giving us players MORE choice!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">At the end of the day, what works in <b>YOUR</b> story with <b>YOUR</b> players is what matters most. Not what someone on some forum says.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/328-phoenixfire","name":"PhoenixFire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar328_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T13:46:57-08:00","id":50039,"title":"","content":"\u201cI like options\u201d, huh? Nice\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[