ents":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T09:02:31-08:00","id":50727,"title":"","content":"Well, I already threw as much as I could on 1E...Rest assured on 2E...will likely be the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T10:35:27-08:00","id":50832,"title":"","content":"I do hope we get to see, perhaps, the Babylonian pantheon. I've been studying them recently, and it would be really interesting to see how it interacts with the modern era. Mind you, I've been also noticing an upswing in the resurrection of old faiths, so seeing that integrated would be kind of cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T11:29:29-08:00","id":50878,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tashiro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=50832#post50832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do hope we get to see, perhaps, the Babylonian pantheon. I've been studying them recently, and it would be really interesting to see how it interacts with the modern era. Mind you, I've been also noticing an upswing in the resurrection of old faiths, so seeing that integrated would be kind of cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded!<br /> <br /> The Annuna are quickly becoming one of my very favorite Pantheons. Not only do they deserve to be in this game by simple virtue of being the oldest recorded religion in history, but they're just choc-full of really powerful and interesting Gods and their mythology is truly fascinating.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'll understand if the Annuna aren't in Hero, but if Mr. Carriker DOES get to introduce several new Pantheons in Demigod and God, or even in a separate supplemental book, then the Annuna deserve to be one of the first Pantheons to be considered for the slot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T12:22:45-08:00","id":50939,"title":"","content":"Amen! So to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T11:22:22-08:00","id":55571,"title":"","content":"This can't happen soon enough!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2073-mctroll","name":"McTroll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2073_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T01:14:20-08:00","id":58575,"title":"","content":"I find the prospect of playing a dryad or naiad or an oread or lampad and deciding to become not just a clay piece on a board played by gods but a god herself immensely interesting. So, I will do that.<br /> <br /> Also, werewolves and vampires and so on being in it and playable as well as antagonist material is awesome. I look forward to those kinds of options, too. &quot;Silver bullet? Seriously?&quot; *voice drops an octave, takes on a guttural growling undertone* &quot;Ever hear of a god named Tyr? You have something in common with him....&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T21:02:24-08:00","id":63274,"title":"","content":"Considering my setting was an amalgamation of the Dresden Files and the WoD.. complete with Faeries, Vampires and a Werewolf trying to be the new Native American War God.. I am so excited..<br /> <br /> Origin looks to be a great addition to the line.. especially the ability to beef up followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2164-mistershifter","name":"MisterShifter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T21:05:26-08:00","id":63275,"title":"","content":"Yup, my Scion was a amalgam of Urban Arcana WoD plus Scion. Origins is the best thing announced so far imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T02:32:29-08:00","id":63355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=58575#post58575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, werewolves and vampires and so on being in it and playable as well as antagonist material is awesome. I look forward to those kinds of options, too. &quot;Silver bullet? Seriously?&quot; *voice drops an octave, takes on a guttural growling undertone* &quot;Ever hear of a god named Tyr? You have something in common with him....&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You will love and cherish them, being the only person who would play with them or bring them food, until your friends force you to betray them because you just won't stop growing? Or did I completely misunderstand the reference? I am so lost!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","user":"Charles Red","date":". 02-02-2014, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T07:09:17-08:00","id":63416,"title":"","content":"Not quite. For a while, you will be the most important member of your group, until some one-eyed prat comes along with some cool magic tricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T08:55:30-08:00","id":69863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=870#post870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now a Caananite Pantheon, that has Baal, Dagon, Moloch, Astarte, etc, that could be really cool. But a Pantheon of Lucifer, Jesus, Mary, Gabriel, etc? No, no thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually what would be a better option is to simply use the Canaanite/El Pantheon and the Abrahamic God is Yahweh which the Angels he has are simply his extensions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","name":"DeathPathoes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T13:50:27-08:00","id":70019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=69863#post69863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually what would be a better option is to simply use the Canaanite/El Pantheon and the Abrahamic God is Yahweh which the Angels he has are simply his extensions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been discussed extensively in the \u201cAbrahamic Pantheon\u201d thread.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=70047#post70047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that scion can't have Yahweh, but what about his prophets + priests? You could simply keep them at the &quot;slightly above mortals&quot; stage until they decide to leave the world and/or go to the underworld/over-world.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=70087#post70087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where would they get their power from? As soon as you bring in any supernatural element to monotheism, you have to start dealing with the supernatural element of it, which causes all the conflicts.</div> </div> </div> </div>So has this. Can we please keep it there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-11-2014, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T14:35:17-08:00","id":70047,"title":"","content":"I know that scion can't have Yahweh, but what about his prophets + priests? You could simply keep them at the &quot;slightly above mortals&quot; stage until they decide to leave the world and/or go to the underworld/over-world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T15:34:22-08:00","id":70087,"title":"","content":"Where would they get their power from? As soon as you bring in any supernatural element to monotheism, you have to start dealing with the supernatural element of it, which causes all the conflicts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T16:00:57-08:00","id":70103,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda late to the party, but are there any system spoilers? I'm not looking for anything big (turn or tick based, attribute spreads and the like), but I never got into old Scion because of the system, though I loved the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T16:36:57-08:00","id":70129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite. For a while, you will be the most important member of your group, until some one-eyed prat comes along with some cool magic tricks.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's Odin to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T10:36:33-08:00","id":72065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>romanov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=70103#post70103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda late to the party, but are there any system spoilers? I'm not looking for anything big (turn or tick based, attribute spreads and the like), but I never got into old Scion because of the system, though I loved the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave Brookshaw has mentioned elsewhere that he's prototyped the new Legend system wherein you can see a familial line of descent from Zeus to Ares to Eros, but the Scion is hardly a clone of the God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1516-solarious","name":"Solarious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T07:42:49-08:00","id":72619,"title":"","content":"So are gods seen through a christian lens the same as supporting monotheism? i'm inclined to say yes. and what about christian legends that became something more? (like leviathan, for example)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T09:12:46-08:00","id":72656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=72619#post72619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are gods seen through a christian lens the same as supporting monotheism? i'm inclined to say yes. and what about christian legends that became something more? (like leviathan, for example)</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a really interesting question.<br /> For one of the myriad &quot;Scion &amp; Christianity&quot; threads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T13:27:36-08:00","id":72799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solarious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=72065#post72065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave Brookshaw has mentioned elsewhere that he's prototyped the new Legend system wherein you can see a familial line of descent from Zeus to Ares to Eros, but the Scion is hardly a clone of the God.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I'm okay to describe it in more detail, but Scions and Gods are treated the same way. Your Origin (whether it's &quot;God-born son of Nyx and Chronos&quot;, &quot;God-born daughter sprung from the brow of Zeus&quot;, &quot;Scion born of Ares and a mortal&quot;, or &quot;Scion adopted by Aphrodite&quot;) influences but does not completely determine your powers. It's one ingredient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T13:41:58-08:00","id":72803,"title":"","content":"Huh. So is God-born set to be a character option?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 02-15-2014, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T18:30:55-08:00","id":72918,"title":"","content":"*rubs hands gleefully*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T22:16:32-08:00","id":73008,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry I'm kinda new to the forum but very interested in Scion. But what's so wrong about a &quot;Pantheon&quot; of the Seven Archangels? They each have their own niche Michael is a warrior, Gabriel is a messenger, Raphael is a healer, Uriel is a attributed to the Sun. They could fit in very easily with Purviews &amp; such. Anyone who is touchy about the Scions being direct descendants could just explain more as being chosen to do the Angel's work.<br /> <br /> If not them then perhaps the Grigori? Azazel &amp; his ilk. Though I would say that they make better use as replacements for the Titans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T22:44:32-08:00","id":73026,"title":"","content":"Thing is, bringing up the subject of Christianity in Scion in a thread has a habit of swallowing the thread whole, which's the last thing we want in a thread about Origin and previews in general. Have a look for the 'Abrahamic pantheon?' thread further down the forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T00:26:36-08:00","id":73067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=72799#post72799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> does not completely determine your powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I could ask for some more explanation but it worked that way, even in Scion 1\u00b0, didn't it? Even a Scion of Aphrodite could use Purviews.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T07:28:47-08:00","id":73175,"title":"","content":"On scion origin don't know if it has mentioned before or not (last time I saw the question appear it wasn't answered as far as I know):<br /> Anything known if there will be previews of things before the game comes out like it was with the latest nwod things?<br /> (thus like in demons or vampire)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T09:19:42-08:00","id":76327,"title":"","content":"Good! I'm really happy to see that PCs can be more than 'child of a god and a mortal', and that the 2e isn't going to have the gods all be unfaithful, having affairs willy nilly. And it allows for some interesting variants - ala Percy Jackson, where a virgin goddess can have a child without actually having sex and without adoption. I'm very, very happy for this. I think, perhaps, that was <i>the</i> big thing that pissed me off with 1e Scion - the idea that for some reason most of the gods completely ignored concepts like 'fidelity'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T12:52:05-08:00","id":76504,"title":"","content":"Well, at least a few pantheons were not exactly overflowing with marital fidelity in the actual myths, but it would be good to have other options, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T14:41:34-08:00","id":76590,"title":"","content":"Someone mentioned before that there might speculative 'minor' beings (Nyiads, Dryads, Djinn(?) ( Water,Tree &amp; FIRE!) spirits as playable characters, since they in some mythos are children of gods themselves... could they too ascend through the rankings of Hero-Demigod &amp; finally God? ( Actually that could be quite intereting if there are some modern Nyiads ect.. or Satyrs... even living in the world as 'mortals'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/205-songtress","name":"Songtress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar205_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T15:30:02-08:00","id":76643,"title":"","content":"While I applaud the decision to broaden the scope of the game beyond \u201cchildren of unions of a god and a mortal\u201d, I hope that that option won\u2019t end up getting sidelined by the alternatives. I like the focus on (though not the exclusivity of) people with a foot in both the worlds of the fantastic and the mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T21:58:05-08:00","id":76869,"title":"","content":"I know my sister would get a kick out of it - she's got a dryad fixation, and would love to see a dryad ascend to a greater role. I'm looking forward to converting my Grigori pantheon to 2e, and possibly my Illuminati pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}